## Evidence

Open work migrated from the canonical TODO. Add implementation and
validation evidence here as the task advances.

September 5 world-preview investigation isolated apparent transparent walls and
missing ground as presentation defects rather than evidence of deleted source
geometry. The original `RenderFlow::DoAllRegistration` sets PDDI culling to
`PddiCullNone`; the OpenGL PDDI backend implements that state by disabling
`GL_CULL_FACE`. Pure3D's simple-material `2SID` parameter can temporarily
disable culling when it was enabled, but ordinary world rendering already starts
from the no-cull state.

The `l1z1` Simpson-house shaders are opaque (`has_translucency=0`, `BLMD=0`)
and not individually two-sided (`2SID=0`), so their apparent transparency in the
native preview is not source-authored translucency. The preview importer also
intentionally disables FBX material and texture import, leaving Unreal's
one-sided default material in the slots. The world catalog now records the
source-backed regular-scene no-cull contract so native world material families
can reproduce it without changing topology. This additive contract advances the
next generated world catalog to `shar.world-package-collection.v7`; the accepted
historical `v6` artifact remains valid evidence for its earlier topology scope.

Ground geometry is present in the source package. Grass, road, sidewalk,
driveway, and asphalt material groups contribute 1,324 triangles in `l1z1`.
The Unreal-target topology sidecar omits only 13 source triangles across the
entire zone (11 zero-area and two repeated-index), with just one zero-area
omission in the sampled grass track. Do not add a replacement
floor or duplicate/backflip faces to compensate for the current preview.
